ption: \"Characteristics: See following page(s)\" — not really a description. I could put null. Maybe description from Table 1? I'll omit or use null. I'll omit.\n\nmodule_designation: For R117 transducer, module designation is \"Not applicable\"? The cert doesn't mention modules. Omit (rule 8).\n\nComponents roles: \"measurement sensor\" and \"electronics\" (two: MVD series electronics, 5700 electronics). Are the two electronics alternatives (OR)? The cert doesn't state. The report table groups them separately, suggesting the transducer can have either MVD series or 5700 electronics. It's plausible they're alternatives but not stated in this fragment. I'll not set \"alternatives\" (null/omit) — safer. Actually within MVD series electronics, MVD700 and MVD800 are two variants. I'll list type_designations: [\"MVD700\", \"MVD800\"] for MVD series.\n\nComponent characteristics: documentation_folder: \"TC7056-14\" etc.\n\nNow model_level entries:\n\n1. maximum_flow_rate (kg/min): models CMF010y 1.8, CMF025y 36, CMF050y 110, CMF100y 450.\n2. minimum_flow_rate_mvd700_class_0_3 (kg/min)\n3. minimum_flow_rate_mvd700_class_0_5_1_0_1_5\n4. minimum_flow_rate_mvd800_class_0_3\n5. minimum_flow_rate_mvd800_class_0_5\n6. minimum_flow_rate_mvd800_class_1_0_1_5\n7. minimum_measured_quantity (kg)\n8. maximum_pressure (bar(g))\n\nHmm, attribute naming with \"class_0_5_1_0_1_5\" is clunky. Alternative: \"minimum_flow_rate_mvd700_accuracy_class_0_3\". Let me use that pattern:\n- minimum_flow_rate_mvd700_accuracy_class_0_3\n- minimum_flow_rate_mvd700_accuracy_class_0_5_1_0_1_5\n- minimum_flow_rate_mvd800_accuracy_class_0_3\n- minimum_flow_rate_mvd800_accuracy_class_0_5\n- minimum_flow_rate_mvd800_accuracy_class_1_0_1_5\n\nOK.\n\nAlternatively, use config_level with axis \"electronics/accuracy_class\" and include model in each value? config values have {condition, value} only — could put condition \"MVD700, class 0.3, CMF010y\"? That duplicates. I'll stick with model_level.\n\nFor the dual values with H/L/M/P: value string \"0.033 (H, L, M) / 0.067 (P)\", footnote_markers: [\"H, L, M\", \"P\"]. Hmm, but actually maybe better to keep the superscript letters as footnote markers on the value and value as the two numbers... I'll keep the string form. Actually wait — maybe cleaner: since H, L, M vs P are unknown conditions, represent as string. Fine.\n\nAlso type_level: should \"maximum_flow_rate\" also be type_level? No, it varies by model → model_level only.\n\nEnvironmental classes: \"M3 / E2+E3 / H3\" — value string.\n\nIntended measurement fluids: attribute \"intended_liquids\" or \"measured_liquids\". Value string listing.\n\nDensity range: min 400 max 1100, unit kg/m³.\n\nMaximum viscosity: 1080, unit \"mm²/s (cSt)\"? The unit mm²/s. I'll use unit_symbol \"mm²/s\" and maybe note \"(cSt)\" — I'll include unit_symbol \"mm²/s (cSt)\"? Cleaner: \"mm²/s\". I'll add value 1080, unit_symbol \"mm²/s\". And there's a qualifier \"under actual operating conditions\" — could add attribute note. Skip.\n\nAmbient temperature: -40…+55 °C.\n\nLiquid temperature ranges (config_level with axis \"accuracy_class\"):\n- mass measurement: 0.3/0.5/1.0 → -10…250; 1.5 → -200…50.\n- density and volume measurement: 0.3/0.5/1.0 → -10…150 (1.5 blank).\n\nNow, footnote markers on cells: none in Table 1/2 besides H/L/M/P and ◇. The ◇ markers on MVD700/MVD800: I could include in matrix_table rows as footnote markers on electronics. In matrix_tables rows are plain objects; footnotes[] at table level. I'll add footnote_markers not available per row... The matrix_tables schema: name, columns, rows (object per row), description, footnotes[]. I can add footnotes: [{\"marker\": \"(◇)\", \"text\": null}]? Don't fabricate text. Maybe skip footnotes, or note in description that MVD700 marked (◇) and MVD800 marked (◇◇). I'll mention in description.\n\nActually, should I include the matrix table at all? Given model_level fully captures it, maybe include just for fidelity. I'll include it —